# Cross-machine hotkey grammar. See docs/hotkeys.md in the repo root for the
# philosophy and full chord map: SUPER -> ctrl+alt, +shift -> +shift, and any
# extra alt/ctrl -> +cmd.
#
# Division of labour: skhd binds yabai actions and nothing else. Anything
# macOS can already do on its own -- switching desktops, screenshots -- is
# configured in System Settings > Keyboard > Keyboard Shortcuts instead, and
# anything an app owns (Alfred's clipboard history and quick actions, Wispr
# Flow's push-to-talk) is set as that app's own global hotkey. Those chords
# are deliberately absent here so they pass through. docs/hotkeys.md section 4
# lists which chord lives where.
#
# Everything below runs through the public Accessibility API, so none of it
# needs the scripting addition. See docs/hotkeys.md section 5 for the one
# Omarchy flow that has no Mac counterpart as a result (send window to
# workspace N), and for how throw-to-display.sh works around the other.

# -- Layout --

# monocle <-> dwindle (stack <-> bsp), mirrors Omarchy's SUPER+M
ctrl + alt - m : ~/.config/yabai/toggle-layout.sh

# rotate layout clockwise, mirrors Omarchy's SUPER+R
ctrl + alt - r : yabai -m space --rotate 270

# -- Displays --

# send window to the next display and tile it there, mirrors Omarchy's SUPER+D.
# macOS's "Move left/right a space" must stay unbound from ctrl+alt - c/d for
# this to reach skhd; see docs/hotkeys.md section 6.
ctrl + alt - d : ~/.config/yabai/throw-to-display.sh

# -- Focus --

ctrl + alt - h : yabai -m window --focus west
ctrl + alt - j : yabai -m window --focus south
ctrl + alt - k : yabai -m window --focus north
ctrl + alt - l : yabai -m window --focus east

# -- Swap --

# swap the focused window with its neighbour. Arrows rather than hjkl so that
# "look over there" (hjkl) and "move the window over there" (arrows) stay
# distinct on one hand. Tiling layouts only -- see docs/hotkeys.md section 5.
ctrl + alt - left  : yabai -m window --swap west
ctrl + alt - down  : yabai -m window --swap south
ctrl + alt - up    : yabai -m window --swap north
ctrl + alt - right : yabai -m window --swap east
